## CSS Variables (Custom Properties)

### Theme Variables

```css
/* shared/ui/theme.css or global.css */
:root {
  --color-primary: #0070f3;
  --color-secondary: #7928ca;
  --color-background: #ffffff;
  --color-text: #000000;
  --spacing-small: 8px;
  --spacing-medium: 16px;
  --spacing-large: 24px;
  --border-radius: 8px;
  --font-size-base: 16px;
}

[data-theme='dark'] {
  --color-background: #000000;
  --color-text: #ffffff;
}
```

### Using CSS Variables

```css
.card {
  background-color: var(--color-background);
  color: var(--color-text);
  padding: var(--spacing-medium);
  border-radius: var(--border-radius);
}
```

## Responsive Design

### Mobile-First Approach

```css
.card {
  padding: var(--spacing-small);
  font-size: 14px;
}

@media (min-width: 768px) {
  .card {
    padding: var(--spacing-medium);
    font-size: 16px;
  }
}

@media (min-width: 1024px) {
  .card {
    padding: var(--spacing-large);
    font-size: 18px;
  }
}
```

### Breakpoint Variables

```css
:root {
  --breakpoint-sm: 640px;
  --breakpoint-md: 768px;
  --breakpoint-lg: 1024px;
  --breakpoint-xl: 1280px;
}

@media (min-width: var(--breakpoint-md)) {
  .card {
    /* ... */
  }
}
```

## Composition Patterns

### Composing Styles

```typescript
// Base component
import baseStyles from './base.module.css';
import componentStyles from './component.module.css';

export function Component() {
  return (
    <div className={clsx(baseStyles.container, componentStyles.specific)}>
      Content
    </div>
  );
}
```

### Style Inheritance

```css
/* base.module.css */
.base {
  padding: var(--spacing-medium);
  border-radius: var(--border-radius);
}

/* component.module.css */
.component {
  composes: base from './base.module.css';
  background-color: var(--color-primary);
}
```

## Animation Patterns

### CSS Transitions

```css
.card {
  transition: transform 0.2s ease, opacity 0.2s ease;
}

.card:hover {
  transform: translateY(-4px);
  opacity: 0.9;
}
```

### CSS Animations

```css
@keyframes fadeIn {
  from {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(10px);
  }
  to {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
}

.fade-in {
  animation: fadeIn 0.3s ease-out;
}
```

## Accessibility in CSS

### Focus States

```css
.button:focus-visible {
  outline: 2px solid var(--color-primary);
  outline-offset: 2px;
}

.button:focus:not(:focus-visible) {
  outline: none;
}
```

### Reduced Motion

```css
.card {
  transition: transform 0.2s ease;
}

@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .card {
    transition: none;
  }
}
```

## CSS Module Best Practices

### Keep Styles Scoped

```css
/* ✅ Good - scoped to component */
.card {
  /* ... */
}

.card-title {
  /* ... */
}

/* ❌ Bad - global styles (use :global() if needed) */
:global(.global-class) {
  /* Only when absolutely necessary */
}
```

### Avoid Deep Nesting

```css
/* ✅ Good - flat structure */
.card {
  /* ... */
}

.card-header {
  /* ... */
}

.card-title {
  /* ... */
}

/* ❌ Bad - deep nesting */
.card {
  .header {
    .title {
      /* ... */
    }
  }
}
```

### Use Semantic Class Names

```css
/* ✅ Good - semantic */
.card {
  /* ... */
}

.card-header {
  /* ... */
}

/* ❌ Bad - presentational */
.red-box {
  /* ... */
}

.big-text {
  /* ... */
}
```

## CSS Modules Checklist

- [ ] Use kebab-case for CSS Module files
- [ ] Match component name in file name
- [ ] Use kebab-case for class names
- [ ] Use clsx for conditional classes
- [ ] Keep styles scoped to components
- [ ] Use CSS variables for theming
- [ ] Implement mobile-first responsive design
- [ ] Add focus states for accessibility
- [ ] Respect prefers-reduced-motion
- [ ] Avoid deep nesting
- [ ] Use semantic class names
- [ ] Place styles next to components